WEBVTT

00:00.540 --> 00:01.373
Instructor: Okie-dokie.

00:01.373 --> 00:02.670
It's time to learn our first command

00:02.670 --> 00:06.210
that has to do with branching and it's a pretty simple one.

00:06.210 --> 00:10.650
It is git branch, git space branch, nothing else.

00:10.650 --> 00:12.360
This will just give us a list

00:12.360 --> 00:15.660
of our current existing branches in a repo.

00:15.660 --> 00:18.240
So it doesn't make a new branch, it doesn't switch branches,

00:18.240 --> 00:21.150
it just shows you the current branches.

00:21.150 --> 00:23.422
In our case, we haven't made new branches

00:23.422 --> 00:26.940
so we won't see anything except master.

00:26.940 --> 00:29.100
So I'm on MyFirstNovel for now.

00:29.100 --> 00:31.050
I'm gonna make a new repository in a moment.

00:31.050 --> 00:35.490
If I type git branch, I see one branch, master.

00:35.490 --> 00:38.463
And to get out of here, just like with git log, I type q.

00:39.420 --> 00:41.340
Now I'll show you a different project.

00:41.340 --> 00:43.800
This repository has a couple more branches.

00:43.800 --> 00:46.770
If I type git branch, you can see them all here.

00:46.770 --> 00:49.500
Birds, birds-of-prey, california-mammals, hawks,

00:49.500 --> 00:53.489
mammals, master, no-animals, owls, stashtest.

00:53.489 --> 00:56.250
(laughs) I was testing something out there.

00:56.250 --> 00:58.620
You can see though there's a bunch of branches

00:58.620 --> 01:03.210
but the one that is active has a little asterisk next to it.

01:03.210 --> 01:05.880
That's the branch we're currently on.

01:05.880 --> 01:08.280
So we see I'm on owls, and again,

01:08.280 --> 01:10.050
I can type q to get out of here.

01:10.050 --> 01:13.230
So here on the the MyFirstNovel project,

01:13.230 --> 01:14.550
we only have master.

01:14.550 --> 01:17.400
I never made that branch, and it's the only branch we have

01:17.400 --> 01:18.600
so we're on it.

01:18.600 --> 01:20.160
We don't really have a choice right now

01:20.160 --> 01:22.960
but next up, we're gonna learn how to make a new branch.
